Component names are now validated as iCalendar tokens when parsing iCalendar (:rfc:`5545#section-3.6`) and as lowercase tokens when parsing jCal (:rfc:`7265#section-3.3`). The value of a ``BEGIN`` line was kept verbatim and used as the XML element name in :meth:`~icalendar.cal.component.Component.to_xcal`, so a name containing ``<`` or ``>`` injected elements into the xCal output and produced XML that is not well-formed. An invalid name now raises :exc:`~icalendar.error.ICalParsingError` or :exc:`~icalendar.error.JCalParsingError`. I used AI to assist me with this change. @alhudz
